d 'ESGDICT': module to provide machine-learning generation of the built-in ESG dictionary that qta requires
d
d	  esgdict learns the built-in dictionary that qta uses for
d its keyword-frequency, cosine-similarity and Jaccard methods,   
d instead of requiring the researcher to hard-code the keywords. 
d It reads a corpus of environmental, social and governance   
d (ESG) reports, screens the documents, tokenises the text, and
d returns a dictionary file organised into the four dimensions	 
d Environmental, Social, Governance and General_ESG.  The resulting
d file is passed directly to qta through its esgdictionary()   
d option. 
d
d KW: text processing
d KW: dictionary
d KW: ESG
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261010
d
d Author: Wu LiangHai,  Anhui University of Technology
d Support: email agd2010@@yeah.net
